+++ b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/decisions.md
@@ -13,3 +13,5 @@
 **P-726. The telemetry config builders are nameable, and `Exporters` has one.** `telemetry` re-exports `TracerConfigBuilder`, `MeterConfigBuilder`, `ExportersBuilder` and their state modules `tracer_config_builder`, `meter_config_builder`, `exporters_builder` (`state_mod(vis = "pub")`), so a downstream helper can take and return a builder, as with `AgentBuilder`/`agent_builder`. `Exporters` derives `bon::Builder` with `#[builder(default)]` fields (decision #65: public fields, `Default` and a builder): `Exporters::builder().otlp(true).build()`. Review finding api-6.
 
 **P-727. Correction to P-495: `ExtractorContext::tracer` being crate-internal is the plain mapping, not a divergence.** TS marks `ExtractorContext.tracer` `@internal` (`memory/extraction/types.ts:61-64`), so `pub(crate) tracer` maps it directly; the staged `DIVERGENCES.md` replacement for the `Memory spans` row drops the tracer half and keeps only the missing `memory.extractor` attribute (P-494). A `Logging` row is staged as well: TS `configureLogging`/`Logger` have no Rust counterpart because the crate logs through `tracing`. Review finding api-9.
+
+**P-728. The OTLP exporters post OTLP JSON, as the TS ones do.** TS uses `@opentelemetry/exporter-trace-otlp-http` and `exporter-metrics-otlp-http`, which post `Content-Type: application/json`. `opentelemetry-otlp` now takes `http-json` in place of `http-proto`, and both exporters are built with `.with_protocol(Protocol::HttpJson)` (a programmatic protocol overrides `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL`, which the TS exporters don't read either). One new compiled crate, `const-hex` (through `opentelemetry-proto/with-serde`; its optional `proptest` appears in `Cargo.lock` but is not built); `cargo deny --locked check` passes. This amends P-490 (the blocking client is unchanged). Files: `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `strands-rs/strands/src/telemetry/config/setup.rs`. Review finding parity-13.
