 | api-7 | Fixed: the `setup_tracer` rustdoc states the subscriber ordering rule; compile-checked doc examples on `setup_tracer`, `setup_meter`, `tracing_layer`, `get_tracer`, `get_meter` and `AgentConfig::trace_attributes`; the two TS module examples (OTLP setup, own provider) are in the `telemetry` module doc, guarded for builds without `otel`. The `lib.rs` module-table row already names the OpenTelemetry setup at this tip, so it is unchanged. `cargo test --doc` passes for the eight new examples | this commit |
 | api-9 | Fixed: (a) the "not in this tree yet" notes in `tests/live_telemetry.rs` and `docs/reviews/live.md` are rewritten, and a replacement `PARITY.md` row for `strands-ts/test/integ/telemetry.test.node.ts` is staged; (b) staged `DIVERGENCES.md` replacement of the `Memory spans` row without the tracer half, and P-727 corrects P-495; (c) staged `DIVERGENCES.md` `Logging` row. The module doc of `telemetry` now says the crate logs through `tracing` (api-7 commit) | this commit |
 | api-11 | For the lead (p10fixa owns `telemetry/tracer/memory.rs`): move the two `otel`-only bodies of `current_span_context` and `link_parent` into the `otel_span` module pair of `tracer.rs` (`current_context`, `add_link`) with no-op twins, or import at the top under `#[cfg(feature = "otel")]`. No `pub` item is involved, so there is no signature edit for this track | not changed |
+| parity-13 | Fixed: `opentelemetry-otlp` feature `http-json` replaces `http-proto` and both OTLP exporters use `Protocol::HttpJson` (P-728); `the_otlp_exporter_posts_spans_to_the_endpoint_from_the_environment` now asserts `content-type: application/json` (it failed with the old assertion after the change, so it observes the encoding); `cargo deny --locked check` passes with the one new crate `const-hex` | this commit |
